course: dictionary
lesson: 14294
title: Nought means zero
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nought is a word for the number zero, written as 0. «Nought point five» means 0.5, the number between zero and one. On a number line, nought sits just before one.
explain: Nought is mostly used in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. In «noughts and crosses», players take turns drawing circles, which are noughts, and crosses. In the USA, the same game is called tic-tac-toe.
explain: Look at the words around nought to check its meaning. «Ten has one ten and nought ones» tells you the ones place is empty, so it is zero. In a maths problem, nought means the value is zero.
fact: Nought means the number zero, written 0.
fact: «Nought point five» is written 0.5.
fact: «Noughts and crosses» is the game called tic-tac-toe in the USA.
fact: In maths, nought means the value is zero.
fact: Nought is a noun: a nought, noughts.
fact: Naught is another spelling that means nothing, but it is mostly found in old or literary writing.
exercise: «Ten has one ten and nought ones.» What does nought mean here? | A hundred | One | *Zero | Ten
exercise: How is nought point five written as a number? | 5.0 | 50 | *0.5 | 0.05
exercise: In «noughts and crosses», what are the noughts? | Stars | *Circles | Squares | Crosses
test: «The temperature fell to nought degrees.» What does nought mean? | Minus one | One hundred | *Zero | Ten
test: Which game is called tic-tac-toe in the USA? | Hopscotch | Snakes and ladders | Kick the can | *Noughts and crosses
exam: «The bank balance was nought pounds.» What does nought mean? | A hundred pounds | One pound | Four pounds | *Zero pounds
